# simple-gin smoke test. nvim + kulala.nvim.
# {{host}} from @host below. <Space>ra sends all, <Space>rr sends one.
# Capture scripts use client.global.set to write the id into
# {{product_id}}, which is read by the GET / PATCH / DELETE blocks.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 0) Health check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### 1) Create a product — captures {{product_id}} from data.data1
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
  client.global.set("product_id", response.body.data.data1);
%}

{
  "name": "Espresso Beans 1kg",
  "description": "Single-origin Ethiopian roast",
  "sale_price": 24.50,
  "price": 29.90
}

### 2) Create a minimal product — overwrites {{product_id}}
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
  client.global.set("product_id", response.body.data.data1);
%}

{
  "name": "Plain Mug",
  "price": 9.99
}

### 3) List products, no filter — paginated response
GET {{host}}/product

### 4) List products, limit 1 — exercises pagination cursor
GET {{host}}/product?limit=1

### 5) List products, filter by name (case-insensitive contains)
GET {{host}}/product?name=espresso

### 6) List products, filter by price range
GET {{host}}/product?min_price=10&max_price=100

### 7) List products, combined filter + pagination
GET {{host}}/product?name=espresso&limit=10

### 8) Get by id — uses {{product_id}}
GET {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}

### 9) Patch by id — change only the price
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 31.50
}

### 10) Patch by id — null out description and sale_price
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": null,
  "sale_price": null
}

### 11) Patch by id — invalid (negative price), expect 422 INVALID_PRICE
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": -1
}

### 12) Patch by id — invalid (name too long > 200 chars), expect 422 INVALID_NAME
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "this is a very long name that exceeds the two hundred character limit imposed by the module to keep query indexes happy and to prevent the persistence of multi-megabyte string payloads in a single column of the products table this is the end"
}

### 13) List with invalid limit (limit=999), expect 422 INVALID_LIMIT
GET {{host}}/product?limit=999

### 14) List with invalid price range (min > max), expect 422 INVALID_PRICE_RANGE
GET {{host}}/product?min_price=100&max_price=10

### 15) Get by id — non-existent, expect 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
GET {{host}}/product/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 16) Delete by id — soft delete, expect 204
DELETE {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}

### 17) Get by id after delete — expect 404 (soft-deleted is invisible)
GET {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}

### 18) Delete by id again — idempotent, expect 204
DELETE {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}

### 19) Patch a non-existent id, expect 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{host}}/product/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 1
}

### 20) Prometheus metrics — expect text/plain
GET {{host}}/metrics
